---
import CaseStudy from "../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/Callout.astro";
---

<CaseStudy
  title="The Great Circle — case study — quentin vanderlinden"
  description="Frontend and desktop decision-support tools for sailors, plus the backend and weather-data pipelines behind them."
  heading="Decision-support tools for sailors, amateur to pro"
  crumb="the great circle"
  tags={["react", "mapbox", "electron"]}
  glance={{
    client: "The Great Circle — Rixensart",
    year: "2016 – 19",
    duration: "~2.2 years",
    role: "fullstack — employee",
  }}
  stack={[
    "react",
    "redux",
    "mapbox",
    "electron",
    "node.js",
    "express.js",
    "typescript",
    "linux",
    "heroku",
  ]}
>
  <p>
    At <strong>The Great Circle</strong>, I spent most of my time building the frontend
    web (and desktop, via Electron) applications that help sailors make decisions —
    from weekend amateurs to professionals.
  </p>
  <p>
    Around the frontends, I built the backend services to pair with them, designed or
    played with algorithms when the occasion arose, and put together the data pipelines
    that pulled in and reshaped the data they ran on.
  </p>
  <h3>Weather in, decisions out</h3>
  <p>
    A recurring thread was integrating new weather-data sources into the backend:
    retrieval and manipulation pipelines that turned each new feed into something the
    apps could route and reason with.
  </p>

  <Callout slot="rail" tone="info" title="Range">
    The same tools had to serve a weekend sailor and a professional racer — which kept
    the interfaces honest and the algorithms defensible.
  </Callout>
</CaseStudy>
